cards.en:
Every HTML page follows this skeleton:<pre>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html&gt;
  &lt;head&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;My first HTML web page&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;/head&gt;
  &lt;body&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;Hello World!&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</pre><ul><li><b>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</b> tells the browser it is an HTML5 document.</li><li><b>The &lt;html&gt; element is the root element.</b></li><li><b>&lt;head&gt; contains information about the file</b>, such as the page title &lt;title&gt; (shown on the browser tab) and scripts &lt;script&gt;. It is not displayed in the page body.</li><li><b>&lt;body&gt; is the container for all visible content</b> – headings, paragraphs, tables, images, hyperlinks.</li></ul>

