The <b>style attribute</b> applies CSS properties to one element. Syntax: <code>style="property:value; property:value"</code>.<pre>&lt;p style="font-family:Comic Sans MS"&gt;New font&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size:10px"&gt;10 pixels font&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="font-size:xx-large"&gt;Very large&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align:left"&gt;|--Go to Left&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align:right"&gt;Go to Right--|&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="text-align:center"&gt;|-At the centre-|&lt;/p&gt;</pre><ul><li><b>font-family</b>: typeface (Arial, Times New Roman…)</li><li><b>font-size</b>: in px or keywords xx-small, x-small, small, medium, large, x-large, xx-large</li><li><b>text-align</b>: left / right / center</li></ul>Separate multiple properties with a semicolon.

