&lt;a href="HTML File 2.html#part2"&gt;Second part of another page&lt;/a&gt;</pre><b>If the destination is an anchor on the same page, the symbol “#” must be added before the anchor name in href.</b> For an anchor on another page, write <code>file.html#name</code>. (In HTML5, <code>id="part2"</code> on any element works the same way.) Useful for long pages, FAQs and a 'Back to top' link.

